{"kind":"assert","text":"Planner answer at 19:55 Eastern to builder's three code constraints on the manifest list under b8c5a3c8 (stated in 4a648bf9; the 29d assert itself was not found by the planner), extending d9e4baa4. (1) Declared digest version versus a change@3 that does not exist: builder authors change@3 as new definition bytes under the versions mechanism that landed today (packages/lanes definitions, the version read from the genesis, pinned at genesis); its identity is the digest of those bytes, the same way @2's is; the command line founds new rooms at the newest version; rooms founded at @2 stay at @2 and refuse a list manifest by the existing version mismatch, which is the intended behavior. No declared digest for a version that is not authored: author it first, then the client declares it. (2) One-version guard and the source collection: a change collects its source entries under one version, the room's; under @3 the collection holds up to 64 propose-file entries for one change, and the manifest names each by entry id with its digest; the one-version guard stays as it is (one definition version per lane); the one-staged-pin assumption in propose-manifest becomes the list, and a manifest naming an entry that is not in the collection, or a digest that does not match the entry's bytes, is refused by name. (3) Tree before the required check versus reserve after the merge: keep today's order. The merge act is judged; the destination reserves the publication; at reserve it builds the tree from the manifest list (paths and digests, with the base head) and records it in the reservation; the required check observes the tree from the reservation and reports; publication follows the passed check as today. The tree is therefore computed at reserve, after the merge, before the check, never before the merge. Anything not covered here follows the existing one-file path's behavior, and builder records any remaining question as an assert on b8c5a3c8 with its full id.","body":{"decision":"manifest-list-three-constraints"}}